20	  id: 'growth-extract',
21	  frequency: 'daily-1h',           // the 03:00 slot — lessons captured from an already-converged mount (DESIGN §2)
22	  // …and, where the repo dispatches through the work-item queue, the ordering the
23	  // anchor hour only IMPLIES, declared (tasks-dispatch DESIGN §9): this task reads
24	  // a mount `core/update` converges, so it yields while that task's item is live
25	  // this cycle and runs the moment it converges — or rolls. Ignored under slot
26	  // dispatch, where the staggered anchors carry the same intent.
27	  after: ['core/update'],
28	  precondition_signals: ['commits', 'prs', 'issues', 'conversationLogs'],
29	  agent_model: 'opus',                   // generalizing/curating lessons is the heaviest judgment, and the default delivery lands the PR with no human review
30	  expected_outcome: 'merged-pr',            // additive edits to the repo's own local packs; delivered to land per the repo's delivery settings
31	  agent_instructions: 'task.md',
32	  agent_execution_timeout: 2700,            // two source passes plus the prose-to-checks upgrade — generous bound, extreme protection
33	
34	  // TWO independent reasons to run, and the Context says which halves are live:
35	  //
36	  //   (a) a SUBSTANTIVE default-branch change — a bot bump / [skip ci] /
37	  //       nightly-baselining commit advancing main is not a lesson to extract, so
38	  //       `commits.substantiveChange` already applies that classification. This
39	  //       arms the activity half AND means a fresh capture now sits on the logs
40	  //       branch, so the conversation half runs too.
41	  //   (b) a log on the branch is ACTUALLY past retention — aged material to give a
42	  //       final hindsight pass and prune, regardless of activity, so the prune
43	  //       still fires on a quiet repo (a log ages out on wall time, not on the
44	  //       repo changing). (b) tests the AGE, not just "a branch exists and
45	  //       retention is configured": that pair is true on every capturing repo
46	  //       every day, which dispatched an opus agent daily to find nothing prunable.
47	  //
48	  // The activity half is scoped by the substantive shas + touched PR/issue numbers
49	  // passed as binding scope — INCLUDING the PRs merged during the window, whose
50	  // review discussion is usually its richest lesson source. Context is binding
51	  // scope and task.md forbids widening past it, so a merged PR the precondition
52	  // does not name is unreadable to the worker. When only (b) fired, Context says
53	  // so explicitly, so a quiet-but-aged run skips the activity half rather than
